  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partnership for Australia-Indonesia Research (PAIR): Sulawesi initiative</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PAIR Sulawesi is a regionally focused research partnership between Australia and Indonesia co-funded by both governments. The initiatives aims to bridge the gap between research and policy, bringing researchers from Australian and Indonesian universities together with policy makers and community groups. It aims to improve policy outcomes in the Sulawesi provinces through local solutions to shared concerns such as the impacts of climate change to coastal communities and the development of renewable energy for local communities in the provinces.</narrative>
  </description>
